From 986b07a804f9c0e2f0058bd5e8c0af29d063eb86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:03:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02433/11362] [outer-loop] tr87 extended to L3: greedy
 multi-glyph-LHS rewrite matcher

Operator: push on to L3. RE'd the L3 delta from internal state + the win predicate.

L3 is again NOT a translation flag (alter_rules/tree/double all None at L3). It
generalizes the rewrite to MANY-to-many: rules now have multi-glyph LHS
([C3,C3]->[A6,A1], [C1,C5,C1]->[A6], [C7,C7]->[A3]). Reading the win predicate
(bsqsshqpox) shows it is a GREEDY left-to-right matcher: scan the target, take the
FIRST rule whose LHS is a prefix of the remaining target, emit its RHS, advance
both pointers. required_editable now implements exactly that greedy matcher --
ONE function that subsumes L1 (1-to-1), L2 (1-to-many) AND L3 (many-to-many).

- solve_adaptered('tr87',3) -> reached_level=3, offline_reproduced=True (60 actions,
  234 states). cyclic-distance verifier + fresh_env (from L2) carry over unchanged.
- 8 adapter unit tests (L1/L2/L3 rewrite cases, cyclic-distance, unmatchable-target
  -> 1000, length-gap bound, fresh_env); all pass.
- metaharness 60-action replay -> L3; aggregate now 29 levels / 16 games (was 28/16).
- registry: greedy-matcher mechanic + the L4 boundary recorded (greedy gives a
  same-length req at L4 that does NOT win -> a tree/double_translation RHS
  re-expansion twist; verifier returns None->1000 or reaches 0 without a level-up,
  so the search stops at L3 with no false claim).

L4 RE (the second-level RHS re-expansion, the tree_translation branch in
bsqsshqpox) is the documented next step.

